Station: Gokana-street, Bori Metropolis. The subsurface model reveals a five-layer sequence. Resistivity begins at 1420 $\Omega \cdot m$, decreases to 859 $\Omega \cdot m$ in the second layer, and then increases progressively through the third (987 $\Omega \cdot m$), fourth (2246 $\Omega \cdot m$), and fifth layers (34337 $\Omega \cdot m$). 

Applying the curve-type notation: the transition from layers 1-2-3 ($1420 > 859 < 987$) identifies as 'H', while the transitions for layers 2-3-4 and 3-4-5 ($859 < 987 < 2246$ and $987 < 2246 < 34337$) both identify as 'A'. This results in an HAA curve type, which is consistent with the survey classification currently on file.

